export const meta = {
  name: 'map-t6-nonnoetherian-existence',
  description: 'Map exactly where IsNoetherianRing enters the rank-one divisor existence chain and what stage/descent machinery exists to remove it',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Map', detail: 'four parallel readers' },
    { title: 'Design', detail: 'route synthesis' },
  ],
}

phase('Map')

const ROOT = '/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild'

const COMMON = `You are mapping Lean 4 code in ${ROOT} (Lean 4 + mathlib algebraic geometry). READ-ONLY: do not edit files. Report exact declaration names, verbatim signatures with all hypotheses/instance arguments, file:line. Your final message is raw data for another agent.`

const SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    findings: { type: 'string' },
    noetherian_uses: { type: 'string', description: 'Every declaration in scope that requires IsNoetherianRing, and WHY (what the proof actually uses it for)' },
    gaps: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['findings', 'noetherian_uses', 'gaps'],
}

const readers = [
  {
    key: 'cut-chain',
    prompt: `${COMMON}
Trace the EXISTENCE chain of the canonical rank-one divisor and find every [IsNoetherianRing ...] hypothesis and what it is used for:
1. ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0RankOneLocalDivisor.lean — baseOpenRankOneDivisor (line ~328), baseOpenDatumSectionLocalEquations, their picClass/abel lemmas, exists_fin_rankOne_away_divisor_with_abel_evaluation (line ~478).
2. ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/SectionsToDivisorsClass.lean and SectionsToDivisors.lean — sectionLocalEquationsOfFibrewiseRegular and sectionLocalEquations: which needs [IsNoetherianRing B] and WHY (read the actual proof: what lemma consumes Noetherianity — germ regularity from fibrewise injectivity? associated primes? Krull intersection?).
3. ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0RankOnePresentation.lean — exists_baseOpen_evaluation_generator (line ~673): does it need Noetherian? what does it need from the presentation P beyond the datum + the four certificates?
For EACH [IsNoetherianRing] occurrence state: declaration, which internal step consumes it, and whether the statement would be false or just unproved without it.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'stage-machinery',
    prompt: `${COMMON}
Map the finite-stage / datum-descent machinery:
1. ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Cohomology/DatumDescent.lean IN FULL — exists_fg_subalgebra_baseChange_eq (line ~151) and everything else public: what exactly descends (the datum? sections? units?) to an FG subalgebra stage, with verbatim signatures.
2. ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Cohomology/RankOneFamilyCertificatesFiniteStage.lean IN FULL — exists_fg_pairH1_vanishing_stage (line ~135): verbatim signature and its exact base/extension setup (which ring is the stage a subalgebra OF, what is transported).
3. ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Cohomology/GluedSheafH0BaseChange.lean — datumH0BaseChange (line ~229): verbatim signature; is it an isomorphism for ARBITRARY base change or only flat? What other H0/section base-change transports exist (datumSectionBaseChange? sectionsMapTop base change?).
4. Search for existing lemmas descending an H0 section to a finite stage: grep for 'exists_fg' and 'stage' across ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian, list all with signatures.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'divfam-basechange',
    prompt: `${COMMON}
Map DivFamZarAff / LocalEquations base-change and its interaction with picClass and abelDivAffPlus:
1. DivFamZarAff.mapAlgHom / mapAlg: does base change preserve the degree parameter and certificates for ARBITRARY k-algebra maps (no flatness)? File Picard/DivisorFamilyAffMapAlg.lean + DivisorFamilyAffFace.lean; verbatim signature of mapAlg and what IsLocallyCertifiedAff transport it does.
2. picClass_mapAlg / picClass_mapAlgHom exact statements.
3. abelDivAffPlus_mapAlgHom exact statement (Picard/DivisorFamilyAffAbel.lean:125).
4. Is there an existing lemma: divisor family over a SUBALGEBRA stage A0 of E base-changed to E has picClass = CechPic.map (relCurveMap C A0 E) of the stage picClass — i.e. can I push a cut divisor from a Noetherian stage up to the carrier and keep class control? Give the exact chain of lemmas.
5. The étale-witness descent: Picard/Pic0RankOneCanonicalDivisorDescent.lean existsUnique_abel_divFamZarAff_of_etale_witness — verbatim signature; confirm it has NO Noetherian hypothesis (only the finite-glue consumer has one).`,
  },
  {
    key: 'presentation-fields',
    prompt: `${COMMON}
Read ${ROOT}/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/Pic0RankOnePresentation.lean lines 1-200 and 600-860 carefully:
1. What derived data does a PicRankOneLocalPresentation P expose over its carrier (datumSection? evaluation? canonicalEvaluation?) — list every def/theorem in the file with a one-line description and which need [IsNoetherianRing].
2. exists_baseOpen_evaluation_generator (line ~673-702): FULL verbatim statement including the evaluation-counit identity conjunct. What produces the generator y — which certificate/module lemma?
3. datumSectionBaseChange (line ~630 area): full signature — how does a section base-change to Localization.Away?
4. datum_classDeg_baseChange (line ~847-856): full verbatim statement.
5. Does ANY existing declaration state 'exists an Abel-correct DivFamZarAff over the carrier' or 'over the test algebra' WITHOUT Noetherian? grep 'abel' in Pic0RankOneLocalDivisor.lean and Pic0RankOneFibrePresentedProducerFiniteGlue.lean and list what exists.`,
  },
]

const results = await parallel(readers.map(r => () =>
  agent(r.prompt, { label: `read:${r.key}`, phase: 'Map', schema: SCHEMA, model: 'opus' })
    .then(res => ({ key: r.key, ...res }))
))

phase('Design')

const good = results.filter(Boolean)
const digest = good.map(r => `## READER ${r.key}\n### FINDINGS\n${r.findings}\n### NOETHERIAN USES\n${r.noetherian_uses}\n### GAPS\n${r.gaps}`).join('\n\n')

const DESIGN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    verdict: { type: 'string', description: 'Which route is best and why, in 2-3 sentences' },
    route: { type: 'string', description: 'The chosen route as a numbered list of Lean lemmas to prove, each with a precise proposed signature and the existing lemmas its proof will use' },
    risks: { type: 'string', description: 'Where the route could fail; what to check first with the LSP before writing code' },
  },
  required: ['verdict', 'route', 'risks'],
}

const design = await agent(`You are designing the Lean 4 formalization route for "T6: non-Noetherian existence" in the AJCR project at ${ROOT}.

CONTEXT. The uniqueness interface RankOneDivisorUniqueness is now DISCHARGED unconditionally (theorem rankOneDivisorUniqueness in Picard/Pic0RankOneUniquenessDischarge.lean). Existence of the Abel-correct divisor (existsUnique_abel_divFamZarAff_of_localPresentation, hence canonicalRankOneDivisor) still requires [IsNoetherianRing P.cover.Carrier] because the divisor is CUT from a datum section via sectionLocalEquationsOfFibrewiseRegular, which needs Noetherianity. GOAL: existence over an ARBITRARY presentation carrier (arbitrary affine test), i.e. a theorem
  existsUnique_abel_divFamZarAff (P : PicRankOneLocalPresentation pi lam) : ∃! F : DivFamZarAff C A (genus C), abelDivAffPlus C A F = picEtAffineEquiv C A lam.1
with NO Noetherian hypothesis. Uniqueness is free (rankOneDivisorUniqueness). Existence is the work.

CANDIDATE ROUTE (stage-cut-and-base-change): descend the datum + section data to an FG (Noetherian) subalgebra stage A₀ of the carrier E (machinery: exists_fg_subalgebra_baseChange_eq, exists_fg_pairH1_vanishing_stage, datumH0BaseChange), cut the divisor over the stage (Noetherian OK), base-change the cut divisor back up to E with mapAlgHom, and use cechPicClass_baseChange + picClass_mapAlg to keep the class identity, then feed the étale-witness descent (existsUnique_abel_divFamZarAff_of_etale_witness, no Noetherian) with uniqueness = rankOneDivisorUniqueness. Judge whether that route is viable against the reader data below; if a cheaper route exists (e.g. Noetherian hypothesis removable at the cut itself, or an already-landed non-Noetherian producer), prefer it.

READER DATA:
${digest}

Deliver: verdict + a numbered route of lemmas with proposed signatures + risks. Be concrete and cite exact existing declaration names from the reader data.`, { label: 'design:t6', phase: 'Design', schema: DESIGN_SCHEMA, model: 'opus', effort: 'high' })

return { design, digest_length: digest.length }
